# Jekyll Plugins and Extensions

## Core Plugins (from Gemfile)
The site uses several Jekyll plugins for enhanced functionality:

### Content Management
- `jekyll-archives-v2` - Archive pages for posts
- `jekyll-paginate-v2` - Pagination for blog posts
- `jekyll-multiple-languages-plugin` - Multi-language support
- `jekyll-scholar` - Academic citations and bibliography

### SEO and Performance
- `jekyll-sitemap` - Generate XML sitemap
- `jekyll-minifier` - Minify HTML, CSS, and JS
- `jekyll-terser` - JavaScript minification
- `jekyll-link-attributes` - Add attributes to external links

### Content Enhancement
- `jekyll-jupyter-notebook` - Embed Jupyter notebooks
- `jekyll-tabs` - Create tabbed content
- `jekyll-toc` - Table of contents generation
- `jemoji` - GitHub-style emoji support

## Custom Plugins
Located in `_plugins/` directory:
- [cache-bust.rb](mdc:_plugins/cache-bust.rb) - Cache busting for assets
- [details.rb](mdc:_plugins/details.rb) - HTML5 details element support
- [external-posts.rb](mdc:_plugins/external-posts.rb) - External post integration
- [google-scholar-citations.rb](mdc:_plugins/google-scholar-citations.rb) - Google Scholar integration

## Plugin Configuration
Configure plugins in `_config.yml`:
```yaml
# Pagination settings
pagination:
  enabled: true

# Giscus comments
giscus:
  repo: your-repo
  repo_id: your-repo-id
  category: Comments
  mapping: title
  theme: preferred_color_scheme

# External sources
external_sources:
  - name: medium.com
    rss_url: https://medium.com/@username/feed
```

## Custom Liquid Tags
The site includes custom Liquid tags for:
- Citations and bibliography
- Figure and image handling
- Social media integration
- Analytics and tracking

## Development Guidelines
- Test plugins locally before deployment
- Keep plugin versions updated
- Monitor for conflicts between plugins
- Document custom plugin functionality
- Follow Jekyll plugin development best practices

